 "notes": [
  "Marco model (uski sab se zyada li gayi entry: “I will always enter as soon as the liquidity is taken” — LB, phir LB ke andar inducement high/low stab hote hi entry, stop LB ke paar, target wo liquidity jo move ne chhodi). 5m preset (daily bias, IE grade A+B, IE management): 509 trades, win 20%, -0.10R/trade (pehle 70% -0.14R, unseen 30% +0.01R). 15m: 150 trades, -0.22R.",
  "4-candle sniper model (YouTube “The ONLY Entry Model You Need”): 5m 1,164 trades, win 23%, -0.10R (unseen +0.06R); 15m -0.24R. Marco + 4-candle saath: 5m -0.10R, 15m -0.24R.",
  "Marco model ke variants: inducement LB ke neeche bhi allow = 5m -0.12R; daily bias ke baghair -0.10R; IE grading ke baghair -0.13R. Stop sirf 0.1 ATR LB ke paar (jaisa video mein tight) = -0.2 se -0.46R (spread aur wick stop le lete hain), is liye 0.5 ATR / kam az kam 1 ATR rakha.",
  "Matlab: Da Vinci se Marco model behtar hai (5m -0.24R se -0.10R), lekin 4 saal ke data par mustaqil edge ab bhi nahi. Unseen 30% par 5m taqreeban zero (+0.01R), jo itne kam trades par luck bhi ho sakta hai.",
  "IE rulebook test (saari 155 videos se 20 rules, 4 saal, 5 markets, spread ke saath): 5m par saare Da Vinci setups 2,612 trades, win 13%, -0.24R/trade. IE grade A+B: 820 trades, win 14%, -0.17R. Sirf grade A: 270 trades, win 10%, -0.61R. IE management (T1 par 80% + break-even + runner) se bhi result negative raha (T1 = 3R par win 22-25%).",
  "15m par bhi wahi: saare setups -0.21R, grade A+B -0.19R (pehle 70% data -0.02R, unseen 30% -0.59R). Kisi IE variant ne dono hisson (pehle 70% aur unseen 30%) par positive result nahi diya.",
  "Kaunse rules data mein madad karte hain: red-news filter (news se pehle wale setups -0.56R vs baqi -0.27R) aur session filter. Kuch rules data mein ulte nikle: LB ke paar liquidity wale setups (-0.18R) un se behtar the jin ke paar liquidity nahi thi (-0.36R); kal ke bare move ke baad wale din -0.32R ke bajaye +0.02R.",
  "Reference trades: 1 July 2024 gold long (Study 1) software ne wahi nikali aur grade A diya. 2 Jan 2024 gold short (CS 2.0 #1, entry 2070.2): software ka 1m short 2070.0-2070.3 par, grade B.",
  "Marco khud (22 March 2025 webinar): “mera strike rate 35 se 50% hai... jo log 70-80% claim karte hain wo jhoot hai; 40-50% bohot achha hai, high 30s bhi theek.”",
  "Case studies ki videos ke frames dekh kar unke marked trades se milaya. Misaal: 1 July 2024 gold (Study 1) par software ne wahi trade nikali: unki entry 2321.8 / SL 2318.6 / TP 2339.8, software ki 2321.3 / 2318.3 / 2338.4 (RR 5.6 dono).",
  "Win rate target par depend karta hai: 5m NY session par 1R target = 38-45% win, 2R = ~28%, 3R = ~20%, opposing liquidity (RR 3+) = 12-14%. Har ek mein spread ke baad R/trade negative raha.",
  "Case studies wali 1-minute confirmation entry (5m zone + 1m entry, chhota stop): win rate 9-14%, average RR ~9, R/trade negative.",
  "Webinars wala trade management (50% partial 2R ya 1R par, phir stop entry par): win rate 15% se 30-43% ho jata hai, lekin R/trade aur kharab hota hai (misaal: 5m NY session -0.08R se -0.25R, unseen data).",
  "Din mein max 2 trades ki limit se nateeja taqreeban wahi raha.",
  "Costs: har market ka spread (gold 0.3$, EURUSD 0.8 pip, GBPUSD 1.2 pip, US30 2.5, NAS100 1.5) + 0.02R slippage."
